        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks, I have it working now :)\n\nI already searched for the 'tree-sitter' binary, but none of the packages in OpenSUSE have it. I was under the impression it was optional anyway so didn't look any further, my bad.\n(For future reference: you can check the files for the one you linked [here](https://build.opensuse.org/package/show/openSUSE%3AFactory/tree-sitter))\n\nThe solution was indeed what you suggested.\nI ended up installing tree-sitter with: ```npm install tree-sitter-cli```\nIn Neovim: ```TSInstall lua``` (make sure it doesn't hang on 'Compiling parser' message!)\nRestarted Neovim\nCheckhealth vim.treesitter now shows:\n```\n- ✅ OK Parser: lua    ABI: 15, path: /home/bart/.local/share/minimax/site/parser/lua.so\n- ✅ OK Parser: lua    (not loaded), path: /usr/share/nvim/runtime/parser/lua.so\n```\n\nAll errors are gone now.",
